WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.580
Today, we are talking about the Valentine's Day episode.

9
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:29.640
I am so excited for this one.

10
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:30.220
Me too.

11
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.320
I liked this one so much, I watched it an extra time in my prep.

12
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:34.740
I did too!

13
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.740
Just for pleasure.

14
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.340
I did too!

15
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.680
My husband Josh was like, babe, how many times are you going to watch that episode?

16
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.020
I was like, I am really enjoying it.

17
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.500
I think this one sneaked up on me because there are certain episodes that I remember as being favorites.

18
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:47.920
Yeah.

19
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.560
And this one was not on my radar.

20
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.600
And then I watched it and so many memories came back too.

21
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:53.880
So many.

22
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.480
Okay, this is a goodie.

23
00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.400
This is season two, episode 16, written by Mike Schur and directed by Greg Daniels.

24
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.360
I mean, honestly, that's all you need to know right there.

25
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.340
That's like the super team.

26
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.960
Yeah, of course this is a great one.

27
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.620
All right, I'll give a summary.

28
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.640
It's Valentine's Day at Dunder Mifflin.

29
00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.260
Michael has to go to the corporate offices in New York.

30
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:21.420
He has to meet and do a presentation for the new CFO, Chief Financial Officer.

31
00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:22.360
It's a big deal.

32
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:22.980
It is.

33
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.700
And he's going to be there with Jan on Valentine's Day.

34
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:27.420
Oh, no.

35
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.480
Back at the office, Phyllis is overwhelmed by gifts from her boyfriend, Bob Vance, at Vance

36
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:35.180
Refrigeration.

37
00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.940
They just come all day, these gifts.

38
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:37.460
All day.

39
00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:42.000
Pam patiently waits for a gift from Roy that never comes.

40
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.140
No, no.

41
00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.660
And she really dolled herself up.

42
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:46.420
Oh, yes.

43
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.500
That's my fast fact number one, Angela.

44
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:49.340
Do it.

45
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.100
Fan question from Baltimore Ashley.

46
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.980
What was the thought process behind Pam's hair for this episode?

47
00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.240
Was there another special meeting?

48
00:01:58.520 --> 00:01:59.320
I bet there was.

49
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.920
Oh, my gosh, you guys.

50
00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.660
I also got similar questions from Casey McMillan and many other people asking if there was

51
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.240
a special meeting for Pam's hair.

52
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.380
There was more than a meeting.

53
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.080
It was like the Joint Chiefs of Staff came together for your hair.

54
00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:20.740
So the thought process here was that Pam and Jim in this episode, they're going to be a

55
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.800
bit estranged.

56
00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:29.300
So wouldn't it be an extra nail in the coffin for Jim if Pam just looked super duper?

57
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.220
Right.

58
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.700
So we thought, can we please do something different with her hair?

59
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.040
I had a MySpace blog at the time, and I wrote about my hair.

60
00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:47.840
And I said that Kim Ferry and I worked for weeks on different versions of this look.

61
00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:52.860
Well, knowing Kim Ferry like I do, like you do, she must have been so excited because she

62
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.560
was so good at hair, but she never got to do much with our hair.

63
00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:56.940
No.

64
00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.600
Okay, so here's what we tried.

65
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:02.260
We tried a ponytail, a barrette, and headbands.

66
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:08.780
We took a picture of each choice, and we presented them to Greg Daniels, and he went

67
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:12.000
through the photos and had to pick hairstyle, and he picked the headband.

68
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.960
And there were various headbands.

69
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.060
I was going to say, were there 12 different headbands?

70
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:18.480
Yes.

71
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.100
Yes.

72
00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:24.180
So it was, and also ponytails, high pony, low pony, side pony.

73
00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.500
No side pony.

74
00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.140
Well, side pony shows up later at the art fair.

75
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.000
Um, I wore a side ponytail to my prom.

76
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.980
My, I think it was my, my senior year, I did a side pony.

77
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.380
I was not cool, guys.

78
00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.100
You did a side pony to prom?

79
00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:39.560
Yeah.

80
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:41.080
I did a side, who?

81
00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.360
Did you get that done at a salon, or did you do that at home?

82
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.880
No, my mom did it.

83
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:50.220
My mom did it, and that was the year, the year before, we had all had dates, and none

84
00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.020
of us had a good time.

85
00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.140
My group of, like, really close girlfriends.

86
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:53.400
Yeah.

87
00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.760
So that was the year.

88
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.800
The guys thought they were being really cool, and they were like, we're not going to take

89
00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:58.420
dates this year.

90
00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.600
I went to a small school.

91
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.600
And so the girls were like, fine.

92
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.660
And we had the best time.

93
00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.900
Was that your senior prom?

94
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:05.780
Our senior prom.

95
00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.860
I danced in a circle with all my girlfriends with a side ponytail.

96
00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.520
Lady, I did an all-girls prom for my senior prom, too.

97
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:14.000
You did.

98
00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.100
We would have been in the same dance circle.

99
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:16.860
We would have.

100
00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.260
You would have loved my side pony.

101
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.020
I have a card about that fast fact.

102
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:22.840
Tell it.

103
00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.360
I mean, not only is it Pam's hair, Pam is wearing a pink sweater.

104
00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:28.740
Her headband's pink.

105
00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.420
She has a heart necklace on.

106
00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.260
She has pink earrings on.

107
00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:33.160
I mean.

108
00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:34.480
Little pink dangle earrings.

109
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:34.700
I know.

110
00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.020
Like, she came to be noticed.

111
00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:38.680
She did.

112
00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.440
She's, I think, a little lip gloss.

113
00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:41.080
Yes.

114
00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.100
It was a whole look.

115
00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:47.560
I have to say, when I first saw myself on screen, I was a little bit like, oh.

116
00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:48.100
Oh.

117
00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.880
Pam went for it.

118
00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:50.680
Pam showed up today.

119
00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:56.460
And I mean, it's going to play out later in the episode, but like, Roy, come on.

120
00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.120
This is someone who clearly wants a valentine.

121
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:00.120
So clearly.

122
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:00.940
No matter what she says.

123
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:01.580
Okay, sorry.

124
00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.560
Fast fact number two.

125
00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:03.680
Fast fact number two.

126
00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.220
A portion of this episode was shot in New York City.

127
00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:09.460
We got a lot of fan questions about this.

128
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.760
People wanted to know if we, did Steve stand in front of a green screen?

129
00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.240
Did we shoot on the streets of Los Angeles?

130
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.120
No.

131
00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.220
But there's more questions, Angela.

132
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:19.500
Okay.

133
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.780
Fan question from Cora Louise.

134
00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.220
How many crew members came to New York City?

135
00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:29.860
And Guava Aura asked, how long did it take to shoot this episode in New York?

136
00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.380
And was the rest of the cast in California?

137
00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:33.660
Yes.

138
00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:35.280
We did not get to go.

139
00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:35.940
We did not.

140
00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:39.120
We were all pretty bummed because it sounded like so much fun.

141
00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.960
So I reached out to Randall Einhorn, our director of photography.

142
00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.580
Jenna, you know I did this.

143
00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.140
I know.

144
00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.040
And you guys, she wouldn't tell me what he said.

145
00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.780
She's got all this good information about the New York shoot.

146
00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:49.840
And she made me wait.

147
00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.520
Well, this is something we do.

148
00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.940
We both love to like dig up nuggets of info.

149
00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.420
And then we don't tell each other because we want the surprise.

150
00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:57.040
I know.

151
00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.960
So I've been waiting like five days for this.

152
00:05:59.180 --> 00:05:59.230
Okay.

153
00:05:59.240 --> 00:05:59.760
Here we go.

154
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:00.980
So I reached out to Randall.

155
00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:05.340
And he said the crew in New York was just him and Greg and Steve that would go out on

156
00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.660
the street when they would film.

157
00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:06.940
Yeah.

158
00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.260
And in the van, they had like, I think, two crew members that were New York based, like,

159
00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.360
because they had to do things by the rules, you know.

160
00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.380
And our line producer, Kent Zabornak.

161
00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:20.220
But whenever the van doors would open, it would just be Greg, Steve, and Randall.

162
00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.660
He said that this was right at the height of 40-year-old Virgin.

163
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.600
It was the biggest movie in America.

164
00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.580
He said there was a billboard in Times Square where they were filming.

165
00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:34.260
So he said the minute Steve would get out of the van, a crowd would form.

166
00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.780
So he said they had to move really fast and quickly.

167
00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:44.760
And he said he used a Handycam camera, like a basic Handycam camera that you could buy

168
00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:45.300
at Costco.

169
00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.160
Whoa.

170
00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:49.500
It's a really small camera, so not to draw a lot of attention to them.

171
00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:49.880
Yeah.

172
00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.920
Because the minute people saw Steve, literally, he said a crowd would form.

173
00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:57.260
Well, wasn't this also right after his Golden Globe win?

174
00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:57.920
Oh, yes.

175
00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:58.360
Yes.

176
00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.400
It was all of that.

177
00:06:59.560 --> 00:06:59.640
Yeah.

178
00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:00.620
He just won the Golden Globe.

179
00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:04.980
There was a billboard of him in Times Square, and they're going to film on the streets of New

180
00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:05.320
York.

181
00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:05.800
Bonkers.

182
00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:06.580
Bonkers.

183
00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:08.680
Now, this was scripted, though.

184
00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:13.860
They had certain scripted spots, but I know that Steve was also improvising and riffing

185
00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:14.480
at the same time.

186
00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:15.720
It was very loosey-goosey.

187
00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:16.440
That's true.

188
00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:16.980
That's true.

189
00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.080
So I asked Randall, okay, what were some of the things that you know were scripted?

190
00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.640
He said the Rockefeller Center portion was scripted.

191
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.820
He said that Sbarro was scripted, but he said that he's pretty sure when Steve goes into

192
00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.140
the subway and sees a man pooping in the box, that that was improv.

193
00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.820
That was Steve just pooping around.

194
00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.940
But Steve did a lot of improv.

195
00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.500
Whenever they saw something or they had a moment, he would hop out.

196
00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:45.320
There's a tag at the end of the fiddler on the roof, him goofing around.

197
00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.340
That's improv.

198
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:51.140
There's a bunch of deleted scenes of him on the streets of New York that I think are a

199
00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.240
lot of improvisations.

200
00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:53.320
They're fantastic.

201
00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.860
The deleted scenes for this are great, and I'll bring up some more of them later.

202
00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:01.360
And then I said, Randall, is there like a fun story or a memory you have from filming in

203
00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.960
New York that maybe doesn't even have anything to do with the episode?

204
00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:04.900
And he said, yes.

205
00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.100
This is what he said.

206
00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.100
He said the night they got into New York, just him and Steve went to this place called

207
00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.180
Johnny's, and they got beer and pizza.

208
00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:14.240
He said he thought the pizza was pepperoni.

209
00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.880
But he just said it was really special, and they were walking back to their hotel, walking

210
00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:24.200
through Times Square, and he said there were billboards everywhere, a 40-year-old virgin

211
00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.240
with Steve's face like all over the place.

212
00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.040
And the show was getting popular.

213
00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.680
Steve had just won a Golden Globe, so it was kind of surreal to walk through all of those

214
00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.300
billboards of Steve.

215
00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:40.000
And people started coming up to Steve, and Randall said that Steve was as gracious and kind

216
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:44.080
to the first person who stopped him, as he was to the 100th.

217
00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:46.720
He just was so kind and in the moment.

218
00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.840
But that is Steve, you know?

219
00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.920
He is so kind and gracious.

220
00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.840
And Randall just said it was really special, I think, for him and Steve to just have that

221
00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.060
night together like that.

222
00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:57.380
Yeah.

223
00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:00.760
Just grabbing a slice and a beer and being in New York.

224
00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:02.300
I'm sure it felt really cool.

225
00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:03.360
Aw.

226
00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.060
I love that.

227
00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:05.700
I know.

228
00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:06.220
Me too.

229
00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.980
That's one of the cool things about the show where there's some sense of the

230
00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.060
circumstance that brings you to an experience you would not have normally had.

231
00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:14.620
Yeah.

232
00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:15.160
Yeah.

233
00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:15.720
So cool.

234
00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:16.360
So cool.

235
00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:19.940
And Greg and Kent Svornak talk a little bit more about New York in the DVD commentary,

236
00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.260
so if you want to give that a listen.

237
00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:24.500
All right, Jenna, that's my New York City nuggets.

238
00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.780
They were great, and they were worth waiting for.

239
00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:27.300
Thank you.

240
00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.120
I loved them.

241
00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:28.580
Thank you.

242
00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:34.900
Fast fact number three, in this episode, we meet the new CFO of Dunder Mifflin, David

243
00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:35.480
Wallace.

244
00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:36.220
Hey, now.

245
00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:36.900
Hey!

246
00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:37.620
Hey, hey.

247
00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.020
Who's here?

248
00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.060
Hey, now.

249
00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.480
By Andy Buckley.

250
00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.280
There we go.

251
00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.260
Who is in studio with us now.

252
00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:44.900
I'm going to put on the Wallace glasses.

253
00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.200
Put on the Wallace glasses.

254
00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:46.440
Bam.

255
00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.540
Andy, you appeared in 37 episodes of the show.

256
00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:50.900
Yep.

257
00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:51.700
37.

258
00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:52.900
That's crazy, yeah.

